### MediCitas — colección identidad (RF17 / I5)
### Requiere: docker compose up (api :8080, keycloak :6767)
### VS Code / JetBrains: extensión REST Client

@host = http://localhost:8080
@kc = http://localhost:6767
@realm = medicitas
@client = api

### 1) Token recepción norte
# @name tokenRecep
POST {{kc}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{client}}&username=recep-norte&password=recep123&grant_type=password

### 2) Health / ready
GET {{host}}/health

GET {{host}}/ready

### 3) Identidad (JWT + Usuario BD)
GET {{host}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRecep.response.body.access_token}}

### 4) Matriz RF17 para el token
GET {{host}}/permisos
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRecep.response.body.access_token}}

### 5) Pacientes de SU clínica (I5: clinicaId en query se ignora)
GET {{host}}/pacientes?clinicaId=clinica-sur
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenRecep.response.body.access_token}}

### 6) Token plataforma (no lee pacientes)
# @name tokenPlat
POST {{kc}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{client}}&username=plat-admin&password=plat123&grant_type=password

### 7) plat-admin → /me OK (clinica null) ; /pacientes → 403
GET {{host}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenPlat.response.body.access_token}}

GET {{host}}/pacientes
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenPlat.response.body.access_token}}

### 8) Sin token → 401
GET {{host}}/me

GET {{host}}/pacientes
